  "implementation": [
    "Each authority Manager retains at most1024 deterministic HMAC filenames keyed by resource kind and ID. The manager already binds its own installation-secret and database-device/inode/owner namespace. No cached value contains a File, reader, lock or permission.",
    "The optional name map is accessed only with try_lock. Full or occupied metadata falls back to the identical HMAC calculation; there is no new authority wait/refusal. Duplicate scope sorting/write precedence and all scopes remain unchanged.",
    "Every use still checks current database identity and private directory, opens and validates the fresh admission file and passes its exclusive turnstile before reusing any live shared resource reader. File owner/mode/type/link checks, cross-process writer fairness, deadlines/cancellation and partial-release behavior remain intact.",
    "Native SQL version stamps, current credential/Device/Endpoint/membership/audience/expiry checks and fresh complete51-scope admission remain unchanged. No200ms media age, peer count, command bound or decoded-frame threshold was relaxed."
  ],
